Subject: [PATCH] angle: enable native parallel compile on Linux SwiftShader

Vulkan leaves enableParallelCompileAndLink disabled by default, so its native
KHR_parallel_shader_compile extension is absent even though compile/link jobs
and nonblocking readiness queries are implemented. Enable the existing feature
for desktop Linux SwiftShader only. Respect explicit feature overrides and
retain all hardware, Windows, Android and ChromeOS defaults/workarounds.

The Vulkan backend marks compile/link jobs thread-safe. ANGLE already runs
parallel compilation and blob-cache configurations on SwiftShader. Retain
normal job lifetime, failed-compile, cache and post-link warmup behavior; no
extension string, completion result, WebGL accessor or profile field is added.

Add a non-skipping Linux SwiftShader capability/functionality test for both
synchronous and threaded hints, and failed-shader completion. Add an ES3
SwiftShader instance alongside existing ES2 coverage. Existing recompile,
context-destruction and drawing tests execute on this native path as well.

Primary source at ANGLE7df613367a1d4ca9aea9ece344d4580d32d132a9:
- include/platform/Feature.h:143 (default disabled)
- src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_caps_utils.cpp:1353 (native extension gate)
- src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp:7242 (thread-safe jobs)
- src/tests/test_utils/angle_test_instantiate.h:128-157 (SwiftShader coverage)
- src/tests/gl_tests/BlobCacheTest.cpp:610 (parallel SwiftShader cache coverage)
- src/tests/angle_end2end_tests_expectations.txt:1532 (Windows ASAN exclusion)

Chromium79460ebecaa5625e57a5fb679a735659e73dc687:
gpu/command_buffer/service/feature_info.cc:1526 requires passthrough decoding.
References: resources/fingerprints/raw/m4-max-chrome-20260908T163229Z.json,
whose WebGL extension list includes KHR_parallel_shader_compile.

Measured since, on the shipped binary, which settles most of what this patch
used to list as outstanding. On this M4 Max through ANGLE/Metal the extension
is present, as the reference says. Through ANGLE/SwiftShader on the same
machine it is absent, because the feature condition here is Linux-only and
deliberately so — that matches stock Chromium's SwiftShader, whose captured
extension list does not contain it either
(resources/fingerprints/raw/stock-linux-20260907T150627Z.json). So macOS and
Windows software rendering are unchanged and stay stock, and the Windows
comparison this patch waited for is not needed to say that: the Windows path is
the untouched default.

What the enablement does change is Linux software rendering, and there it is a
difference from stock that is worth naming. A Linux host with no GPU that is
served no profile inherits itself, and then offers KHR_parallel_shader_compile
where stock's SwiftShader does not — one extra name in getSupportedExtensions(),
enumerable. Serving a profile removes it, because patch 0028 deletes any
extension the claim does not contain while the native parallel path keeps
running underneath, so the compile speed is kept and the enumeration is stock.
That makes the remedy the same swiftshader-backend anchor patch 0027's prose
asks for, and until it exists this is the one page-visible cost of the speedup.

Still open, and only this: the ANGLE end2end tests added below have not been
run, because this checkout cannot build them.

diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
--- a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -6498,6 +6498,11 @@
     // which can be huge. zlib take long time to compress it.
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, skipPipelineCacheSerialization, isSwiftShader || isNvidia);
 
+    // Use the existing thread-safe compile/link jobs on desktop Linux SwiftShader.
+    // Other platforms and drivers retain their existing feature policy.
+    ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, enableParallelCompileAndLink,
+                            IsLinux() && !IsAndroid() && !IsChromeOS() && isSwiftShader);
+
     // Practically all drivers still prefer to do cross-stage linking.
     // graphicsPipelineLibraryFastLinking allows them to quickly produce working pipelines, but it
     // is typically not as efficient as complete pipelines.
diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/tests/gl_tests/ParallelShaderCompileTest.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/tests/gl_tests/ParallelShaderCompileTest.cpp
--- a/third_party/angle/src/tests/gl_tests/ParallelShaderCompileTest.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/tests/gl_tests/ParallelShaderCompileTest.cpp
@@ -384,6 +384,35 @@
     EXPECT_EQ(8, count);
 }
 
+// Default software support must not turn into a silently skipped capability test.
+TEST_P(ParallelShaderCompileTest, DefaultSupportOnLinuxSwiftShader)
+{
+    ANGLE_SKIP_TEST_IF(!IsLinux() || IsAndroid() || IsChromeOS() || !isSwiftshader());
+    ASSERT_TRUE(EnsureGLExtensionEnabled("GL_KHR_parallel_shader_compile"));
+
+    // Both the synchronous hint and the threaded path must produce real programs.
+    for (GLuint count : {0u, 2u})
+    {
+        glMaxShaderCompilerThreadsKHR(count);
+        ASSERT_GL_NO_ERROR();
+        TaskRunner<ClearColorWithDraw> runner;
+        runner.run(this, kPollInterval);
+    }
+
+    // Completion is distinct from compilation success, including invalid input.
+    GLuint shader = glCreateShader(GL_FRAGMENT_SHADER);
+    const char *invalidSource = "this is not a valid shader";
+    glShaderSource(shader, 1, &invalidSource, nullptr);
+    glCompileShader(shader);
+    GLint status = GL_TRUE;
+    glGetShaderiv(shader, GL_COMPILE_STATUS, &status);
+    EXPECT_EQ(GL_FALSE, status);
+    glGetShaderiv(shader, GL_COMPLETION_STATUS_KHR, &status);
+    EXPECT_EQ(GL_TRUE, status);
+    glDeleteShader(shader);
+    EXPECT_GL_NO_ERROR();
+}
+
 // Test to compile and link many programs in parallel.
 TEST_P(ParallelShaderCompileTest, LinkAndDrawManyPrograms)
 {
@@ -497,7 +526,9 @@
     runner.run(this, kPollInterval);
 }
 
-ANGLE_INSTANTIATE_TEST_ES2(ParallelShaderCompileTest);
+ANGLE_INSTANTIATE_TEST(ParallelShaderCompileTest,
+                       ANGLE_ALL_TEST_PLATFORMS_ES2,
+                       ES3_VULKAN_SWIFTSHADER());
 
 GTEST_ALLOW_UNINSTANTIATED_PARAMETERIZED_TEST(ParallelShaderCompileTestES31);
 ANGLE_INSTANTIATE_TEST_ES31(ParallelShaderCompileTestES31);
